      "page": {
        "title": "Business rules — lodgement checks",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "h3": "Business rules — lodgement checks"
          },
          {
            "p": "The rules behind REQ-01 to REQ-05, written so the build team and compliance read them the same way."
          },
          {
            "h4": "BR-01 Policy match"
          },
          {
            "p": "The policy number must exist, be active on the incident date, and belong to the person lodging. If it doesn't match, the customer can search by name and address. A claim can't be submitted unmatched."
          },
          {
            "h4": "BR-02 Evidence"
          },
          {
            "p": "Contents claims over **$1,000** need at least one photo or receipt per item before submission. Threshold to be confirmed at sign-off."
          },
          {
            "h4": "BR-03 Cover period"
          },
          {
            "p": "The incident date must fall within the policy's cover period. If it doesn't, the claim is accepted and flagged for a claims officer — never rejected automatically."
          },
          {
            "h4": "BR-04 Duplicates"
          },
          {
            "p": "Same policy, same claim type, incident dates within 7 days: warn the customer and show the existing claim. Don't block it — some customers genuinely have two events."
          }
        ]
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "title": "Sign-off meeting — agenda",
          "body": "45 minutes, Helena chairing. Decisions, not discussion.\n\n1. REQ-06 bank details: lodgement or settlement? Triage and compliance get five minutes each\n2. REQ-02 photo threshold: $1,000 (my recommendation) or $500\n3. Confirm live chat stays a Could\n4. Sign off the seven agreed requirements\n\nPre-read goes out @+1d with the current-state findings attached."
        }
